# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so a checkout
# rewrites text files to CRLF. That is invisible until one of them is copied to
# a server and run: a shell script with CRLF line endings fails on the first
# line with "\r: command not found", which reads as a corrupt file rather than a
# checkout artefact. The two kinds of file here that are executed or parsed on a
# Linux host are pinned to LF.
#
# Deliberately NOT "* text=auto": that would renormalise every existing file in
# the repository on the next commit and bury a real change in the diff.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
